From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: 2026-10-11
Subject: [PATCH jm-v9 028] panvk: v9 chunk direct restart strips, size tess chunks on the GPU biblioklept

Purpose: PanProbe large_draw, gs_tess_primitive_id and tessellation
(30 s fence timeout) failed on the G57.
Root causes: (011/017) direct strips with primitive restart larger than
the arena were dropped; the GPU chunker was indirect-only. (014/017) tess
chunks were sized for every patch at level 64: with XFB/GS 2 patches per
chunk, so 70000 patches needed 35000 iterations (cap 4096) and indirect
draws got 8 x 2 patches.
Fix: panlib_chunk_step cut_tail mode (cut after the last restart in the
first half of the window, so each chunk advances >= step/2 and the CPU can
bound the chunk count); v9_prerast_chunked takes a chunk count and direct
draws (cap 1024). panlib_tess_draw sizes chunks from the real levels:
up to 4096 patches per chunk, keeps the longest run that fits the arena
index budget, hands the rest to the next chunk, counts the TCS statistic
for kept patches. Direct tess draws record up to 1024 iterations,
indirect 32. Tess output ranges that fit go straight to
v9_prerast_draw_one. All new fields and kernel logic are under
PAN_ARCH == 9: CSF structs and kernels are byte-identical.
Known limits: postponed patches rerun VS/TCS (duplicate TCS side effects);
output past the caps is dropped with a warning; triangle strips with
adjacency stay unhandled.
---

